
  <sn><md>### Introduction to Carbohydrate Isomerism

Except for **dihydroxyacetone** (ketoses), all monosaccharides contain one or more asymmetric or **chiral carbon atoms**. Because of these chiral carbons, monosaccharides exist in `optically active isomeric` forms.

We will discuss
- Stereoisomers
- D- and L-isomer
- Racemic mixture
- Epimers
- Enantiomers
- Anomers
- Tautomerization
</md></sn>
